e expectations and settings. Type/artifact successes and SDK successes do not waive failed lint, formatting, coverage or runtime jobs. Use the actual pinned tools through authorized GitHub validation; do not claim the final checks pass before they do.\n\n2. Faithful export underlines (Recommended), as a bounded concrete repair-plan strategy.\nThe settled task already requires thin primary/secondary underlines for in-document text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only at end-of-line/empty padding; it forbids hiding or replacing SQL characters. The earlier Six comparisons decision expressly permits a demonstrated faithful export-only underline geometry repair after independent inspection, concrete full-scope plan review and meaningful causal regression. This answer does not select a new terminal primitive or production font.\n\nThe independent resolver inspected every one of the twelve ORIGINAL full stage PNGs individually, plus both full final scene PNGs, and read their exact SVG/geometry/provenance. These are the actual current667 rejected capture, run39264821529, producer author:81c7a96e37494ccb838079e011f61e46, task8e54828510b923a2febe544f388faba9d37eabdf0e3269ccbe62d24fdc3898eb, base04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9. Assigned visual-evidence/manifest.json SHA256 fbfe0ad894e8f08f5fe5ad0d20dcb26a066ab576a2c852f3e7b9b6f2dfa10886; source visual manifest578aef28eeab7030c7eaa69d5a8d6ec4a8fa30f9c932eb90ed693b3cd1f67320; actual visual-rejection.json9b9141965ed2357d070339733f8f3716f8a10ba021f50ca3af655da7fb038329. They are already assigned planning evidence, not a new evidence-tool assignment or fabricated private authority.\n\nFor keyboard-multicursor and editor-command-caret, the original/diagnostic-DejaVu pair is retained at direct1280x800, actual intermediate2560x1600 and one Lanczos reduction1280x800. Both ordinary final scene PNG hashes exactly match their reduced_original counterparts. The steady editor caret is not distinctly visible in the command-focus scene while its command-input caret is visible; neither tested font declaration restores a distinct editor underline at any retained stage. The keyboard scene likewise does not make all three thin caret underlines distinctly identifiable; that diagnostic observation is not an invented extra failed-scene verdict. Static terminal widget/compositor rows and SVG retain the intended underline at the mapped cells: command scene primary period at screen[19,5], document[1,14]; keyboard d/period/t at[19,4],[19,5],[19,6]. SVG text keeps x231.8,textLength12.2, original colors/underline classes and line clips. Command line5 baseline142 is within clip y123.5,height24.65. Correct styling alone is not raster visibility proof.\n\nThis supports a narrow span-derived export representation experiment at the observed SVG-to-raster boundary. It does NOT prove a specific resvg bug, the actual renderer-selected font, a clipping mechanism, a zero-pixel absence or a successful repair. Installed DejaVu/fc-match observations are not selected-font proof. Preserve those uncertainties and both original font declarations. Current agent-review118113179850 actually completed FAILURE at2026-10-19T14:21:16Z, reportb9e599e60147f4aacab4a80615b8494d6c3af59e8025e4c41d4d71b6f32efc55, confirming the missing editor caret Ln2Col15 while command input has focus. Keep this finding effective until genuinely fresh acceptance. Historical0b/e7046 46-scene acceptance is not approval of current667 or this repair.\n\nThe concrete plan must identify the exact export-only helper/function/placement and explain deriving thin underline geometry from actual underlined terminal SVG spans and their resolved style, x/y/textLength, transforms and existing clips. Preserve every original text node, glyph/SQL/whitespace character, foreground/background color, coordinate, width, cell mapping, clip and terminal behavior. Explain vertical placement/thickness, avoidance of duplicate decoration, and safe handling of spans, whitespace, wide/combining characters and clipping; unsupported or ambiguous input must be reported honestly. Do not hardcode scene names, caret coordinates or overlay pixels from diagnostic positions; do not synthesize a caret absent from the actual terminal underline spans. No bars, block masks, text replacement, font switch, layout alteration or guessed assertion update. Preserve raw originals verbatim and explicitly distinguish any new normalized SVG in evidence.\n\nThe actual source seam is agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py _frame_svg/_write_png/_capture_frame and agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py rasterize_framed_svg. Exact current667 source SHA256s are respectively61de7d68e824303b0226c8272c14c62287d26d51985c21942f20b89395f8691c andecb681c49567e9227437d943bf2db8722b1eb9e43a6536ac9da9a68036a7b7ba. The latter currently renders the unchanged complete target frame in a2x outer viewport with resvg_py.svg_to_bytes and performs exactly one Pillow Lanczos reduction. It does not already implement explicit underline geometry. Keep that supersampling/reduction contract and complete retained stage comparisons. Source identities describe existing bytes, not permission to run or activate them.\n\nRequire a meaningful fast actual-raster regression with an unmodified current SVG/export that fails the required caret-visibility check and a reviewed repair that passes it at the actual mapped cells, covering command-focus persistence plus keyboard primary/secondary occupied and whitespace carets. Include meaningful no-underline/wrong-cell/clipping and preservation negative controls; prove text/colors/coordinates/clips/widths remain faithful. A static underline flag, mocked raster, any changed pixel somewhere, transformed expected result or tiny period mistaken for a full caret is insufficient. The concrete full-scope plan and causal regression requirement must receive independent review before implementation; no proposed algorithm or before/after result is approved by this strategy response. If the concrete approach cannot meet these constraints, report the precise limitation and revise the plan without inventing proof.\n\nPreserve the complete original anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns/reversal/clamping/boundaries and same-row multicursors, exact toggle/selection merging; document-order fragments and empty-selection/single-whole-buffer copy/cut rules; fragment then matching-line then whole-text paste across keyboard/command/terminal, metadata invalidation and empty behavior; atomic bounded undo/redo/history/reset. Preserve SQL/whitespace/colors/widths/scroll/ruler/selection/completion mapping and suffixes, native-style equality, mount/restoration/focus ordering exactly once, recovery/journal/help/picker/menu/find/new-file repairs, border/font diagnostics, faithful Unicode/style cropping and all useful checkpoint work.\n\nRequire newly bound twelve complete stage PNGs/SVGs with original and diagnostic-only font controls, exact bytes/hashes/dimensions/font observations/versions/arguments and source/task/plan/base/candidate/run/job/attempt/artifact provenance, then all46 automated geometry checks and individual full1280x800 scene PNG verdicts at208x47 before correction publication. Require separate complete-feature/source/companion review and exact-final-head GitHub quality/lint/format/type/coverage/artifact/compatibility/minimum-dependency/SDK/fast checks. Retain the actual current coverage/subsystem/debt floors, public>=3.8 static compatibility and inherited current-dev3.9–3.14/minimum runtime matrix; do not lower stronger current floors to historical numbers. No skips, retries-until-green, suppressed assertions or old-head receipt transfer.\n\nUse the already established bounded legacy GitHub capture/ordinary CI route for PR9, with current real action-time authorization/security/provenance/producer-consumer/operational guards. Its GitHub-hosted contents:read/persist-credentials:false facts do not establish native/container activation or blanket absence of every infrastructure credential/channel. Preserve inherited PR50/47 native-validation/authority source on actual current dev without activating it. PR45/39 native product gates remain separate; no unactivated native framework, new raw-data publisher, receiver/bootstrap service or adapter becomes a fabricated PR9 dependency. No candidate programs/tests/imports/installs/builds/renders/font probes locally or onPi; source workers remain source-only. No takeover or modification of a handed-off branch by another author.\n\nPreserve all genuine current owner-input/veto/cancel/authentication/security/provenance/protected/operational holds and completed/cancelled history. This is not a hold release, owner personal fact, protected approval, main/runtime activation, source/visual/CI pass, merge clearance or parent-task completion. Session dev-automation approval waivers do not waive CI/security/provenance/visual gates. Preserve #10's actual #9-dev-merge/ancestry dependency, separate #39/#37 scope, companion monitoring through actual successful dev merges, and the full recommendation/restart/recovery/lifecycle/history/orchestrator requirements. Recheck actual request revision/head/base and controls at every real action boundary; a future base change requires genuine revalidation.\n\nExact current questions and every offered option retained with this automated answer:\n\n1. Should the correction complete the fake new-file screen in tests/agent_tools/visual_evidence.py with centered viewport/dialog geometry, resolved alignment and query_one support, preserving every required-element and stale-evidence assertion plus the real mounted centering regressions?\nComplete fixture (Recommended): Repair the six demonstrated fixture failures without bypassing alignment checks or changing production behavior.\n\n2. The inspected stage PNGs and diagnostics locate the command-caret visibility failure between intact SVG underline styling and raster output; neither tested font declaration resolves it. Should the renewed plan use an export-only explicit thin underline derived from actual underlined terminal spans, preserving text, colors, coordinates, clips and terminal behavior, with a real raster visibility regression and fresh full-scene review?\nFaithful export underlines (Recommended): Represent the existing underline as SVG geometry; retain original evidence, supersampling and all twelve stage comparisons, without introducing bars or blocks over text."],"decisions":[{"choice":"ui_repair_scope: Minimum gate repairs (Recommended)\nReason: The later authenticated standing instruction to always use recommended implementation/correction options supports the previously presented minimum gate repairs, superseding the earlier deferral for these listed blockers. Preserve the multicursor requirements and require every full visual scene to pass through GitHub validation.\ncaret_fallback: Preserve text (Recommended)\nReason: The later standing recommendation policy supports this explicitly presented rendering compromise: vertical bars where supported, thin underlines in occupied cells, and readable SQL with visible primary and secondary carets. It supersedes the earlier unconditional vertical-bar preference for this limitation.\nmonitored_pr_scope: Task-related PRs (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy supports the task-related interpretation of ALL PRs. This choice retains the root monitoring objective across SQL Explorer #9, the requested RPi policy/restart companion work, and all related correction or repair PRs until successful dev merge and validation; a leaf repair cannot replace that objective. Protected exact-head approvals remain with the real owner.","questions":["1. Which UI repair scope should the plan retain? Your earlier answer deferred unrelated UI defects; the later questions about broader visual-gate repairs received no direct answer, and partial code cannot establish scope.\nMinimum gate repairs (Recommended): Include only the listed scene consistency/Cancel focus, create-table legibility/type-menu placement, help wrapping, and remaining find-highlight blockers; require the full visual gate.\nFeature and fixtures: Allow multicursor corrections and truthful scene fixtures; defer unrelated production UI repairs even if they block the full visual gate.\nFeature only: Limit corrections to multicursor behavior and visuals; leave unrelated fixtures and UI defects deferred.","2. When a thin vertical caret cannot share a terminal cell with readable SQL, which rendering compromise should the plan use? The earlier “Vertical bar” answer did not resolve this later limitation.\nPreserve text (Recommended): Use a supported vertical bar where possible and a thin underline in occupied cells; show primary and secondary carets without hiding SQL.\nAlways vertical bars: Add presentation-only cells for vertical bars and adjust mouse, scrolling, ruler, selection, and completion mapping consistently.\nBar may cover text: Allow a cell-replacing vertical bar to hide the character beneath it; the legibility gate may remain blocked.","3. Which PRs must reach successful dev merge before the coordinator stops? Supplied evidence identifies SQL Explorer PR #9 and companion work, but does not establish that every open PR belongs to this task.\nTask-related PRs (Recommended): Track #9, the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and their task-related correction or repair PRs through review, validation, and successful dev merge.\nAll currently open PRs: Record a fresh repository inventory and monitor every currently open PR, preserving each PR’s separate scope and approval requirements.\nExplicit PR list: Use the repository/PR list you supply in the free-text answer, plus their task-related correction and repair PRs."]},{"choice":"database_heading_scope: Repair heading (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's later standing instruction to use recommended implementation/correction options, together with 'fix any issues on the way,' supports this narrow heading repair beyond the earlier enumerated boundary. Diagnose the reported obstruction before treating its cause as confirmed; retain the focused regression and complete GitHub visual gate. This leaf repair preserves all multicursor requirements and the root objective to monitor task-related PRs through successful dev merge and validation. It grants no protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Should the plan include a narrow correction for the newly reported database-picker heading, where the initial “c” in “.connections” is obscured, beyond the previously enumerated minimum UI repairs?\nRepair heading (Recommended): Diagnose the widget, compositor and capture evidence; fix only the confirmed text-obscuring cause, add a focused regression, and require the full visual gate.\nKeep prior repair boundary: Preserve the earlier enumerated scope and report the heading as an unresolved visual blocker; publication remains blocked while the scene fails."]},{"choice":"picker_export_repair_strategy: Isolate export defect (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues support this evidence-first correction. The hash-verified PNG obscures the c, while widget/compositor rows and parsed SVG retain the complete heading. Obtaining raw/framed SVG bytes and renderer/font diagnostics addresses the remaining coordinator artifact gap without inventing a production picker defect or claiming those bytes already exist. Correct only the demonstrated cause, retain fast regression coverage and full independent visual review on GitHub, and preserve all multicursor, RPi policy/restart, provenance and task-related PR monitoring requirements through successful dev merges and validation. Lossless publication transport remains coordinator-owned; history must remain complete. Protected exact-head approval remains exclusively with the real owner.","questions":["1. The verified PNG obscures the `c`, but widget rows, compositor rows and the parsed SVG preserve the complete heading with visible styling and a containing clip. Which correction strategy should the revised plan specify?\nIsolate export defect (Recommended): Keep picker presentation intact. Have the coordinator obtain raw/framed SVG bytes and renderer/font diagnostics from a GitHub reproduction, then correct the demonstrated export/rasterization cause and add a fast regression before full visual review.\nPresentation workaround: Investigate a narrow picker text-rendering workaround, requiring evidence that it preserves the complete heading and terminal layout; this may change production presentation despite intact widget/compositor output."]},{"choice":"picker_rasterization_diagnosis: Controlled captures (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and authenticated coordinator instructions support bounded GitHub-only diagnostic comparisons before selecting a repair. Comparing unchanged and framed SVG inputs and an explicitly available monospace font can investigate the unresolved rendering cause without assuming the actual renderer-selected font. Preserve exact inputs, settings, hashes, PNGs, checkpoint and production UI; retain independent review, full-scene validation, complete feature requirements, RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of all task-related PRs through successful dev merges and validation. This diagnostic choice grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. The complete raw and framed SVGs retain the heading, but the PNG remains rejected and the actual renderer font is unknown. Should the next independently reviewed step add bounded GitHub-only comparison captures to distinguish framing/scaling from font shaping before selecting a repair?\nControlled captures (Recommended): Preserve the checkpoint and production UI; compare the same SVG before/after framing and with an explicitly available monospace font, retaining exact inputs, settings, hashes and PNGs for review."]},{"choice":"comparison_artifact_transport: Geometry JSON (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated coordinator explicitly supports bounded, lossless diagnostic content in the already-exported geometry JSON through the existing GitHub candidate-capture route. Extending that route to the selected controlled comparisons preserves exact SVG/PNG inputs, settings and hashes for independent review without changing the protected workflow. Size limits must mark omitted or incomplete evidence explicitly; incomplete comparisons cannot establish a cause or satisfy review. This choice preserves production behavior, the complete checkpoint and history, all multicursor requirements, RPi policy/restart work, full-scene visual and CI gates, and monitoring of all task-related PRs through successful dev merges and validation. It supplies no missing factual evidence and grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. The trusted workflow uploads scene PNGs and geometry JSON, but no extra comparison files. How should the already-selected controlled picker comparisons reach independent review?\nGeometry JSON (Recommended): Retain bounded, lossless comparison SVGs and base64 PNGs with settings and hashes in database-picker.json; the coordinator extracts hash-bound images using the existing artifact route.\nSeparate artifact files: Extend the protected capture workflow to upload comparison SVG/PNG sidecars, requiring fresh independent review and real owner approval for that exact protected head."]},{"choice":"picker_comparison_recipe: Four-way comparison (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated standing recommendation policy and previously selected controlled comparisons support this bounded diagnostic recipe. Supplied font evidence lists DejaVu Sans Mono as available; it does not establish the original renderer-selected font. Run comparisons only in GitHub, changing only the terminal font declaration in diagnostic variants while preserving production rendering and the checkpoint. Retain exact inputs, settings, hashes and lossless PNGs through bounded geometry JSON; failures or omissions remain incomplete evidence. This intermediate diagnosis preserves all multicursor requirements, RPi policy/restart work, full independent visual and CI gates, complete provenance, and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and validation. It supplies no repair verdict or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. For the already-selected controlled picker captures and geometry-JSON transport, which concrete comparison recipe should the next plan specify?\nFour-way comparison (Recommended): Render raw and framed SVG with original font declarations, then both with only the terminal font declaration changed to verified-available DejaVu Sans Mono. Preserve text, positions, clips and production rendering; retain exact inputs, settings, hashes and lossless PNGs in bounded geometry JSON, marking failures or omissions incomplete.\nStage comparisons: First capture raw versus framed SVG with original fonts; independently review those results before planning a second capture with an explicitly available monospace font. This needs another diagnostic cycle if framing alone does not explain the defect."]},{"choice":"ci_correction_strategy: CSS reference (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues support this bounded CI correction. The existing reference already declares color: $text-disabled in CSS; its plain Color.parse override bypasses Textual's CSS resolution. Removing that override while preserving strict resolved/rendered-color comparisons and negative controls aligns with the requirement not to weaken assertions. Behavior-preserving Ruff fixes also align, provided diagnostic output, production UI, the complete feature checkpoint, provenance and validation gates remain intact. Validation must run on GitHub. Preserve the RPi policy/restart work and root monitoring objective through successful dev merges and required validation for every task-related PR. This assessment grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Should this correction use Textual’s existing CSS reference to resolve disabled colors and make behavior-preserving Ruff fixes, while retaining the complete feature checkpoint and all review gates?\nCSS reference (Recommended): Remove the invalid plain-color override; retain strict resolved/rendered-color and negative-control assertions; fix helper/test lint without changing diagnostic output or production UI.\nExplicit CSS parsing: Implement test-side parsing of Textual auto/percentage color values and verify it across supported versions; retain the same strict assertions and behavior-preserving lint fixes."]},{"choice":"ci_fixture_strategy: Complete fixture (Recommended)\nReason: The selector fixture mounts only Select, while create-table diagnostics require #create-table-advanced.collapsed. Mounting a real Collapsible corrects missing fixture context while preserving completeness assertions and the missing-context negative control. Behavior-preserving per-region extraction and formatting align with the authenticated evidence-first correction and standing recommendation policy. Preserve diagnostic contents, assertions, coverage/debt baselines, the complete feature checkpoint, unresolved picker prerequisite, GitHub validation and independent review gates, and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This choice supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Exact-head CI identifies an incomplete selector fixture, a PLR0912 branch-count finding in terminal_diagnostics, and formatting findings in two diagnostic test modules. Which bounded correction should the plan specify?\nComplete fixture (Recommended): Mount a real advanced-panel Collapsible in the selector fixture; preserve every completeness assertion and missing-context negative control; extract per-region collection into a behavior-preserving helper and format the two reported test modules.\nIsolate selector fixture: Stub only checkbox-context collection in the selector-only test, retain real-scene and missing-context coverage elsewhere, and make the same behavior-preserving branch-count and formatting corrections."]},{"choice":"picker_export_correction: Supersampled export (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and evidence-led heading correction support this bounded export strategy. Hash-bound comparisons show intact native-size headings and degradation at target size with either font; preserving SVG interior bytes does not remove the defect. Pillow is already an agent dependency. Supersampling remains a proposed remedy, requiring exact-candidate GitHub reproduction, focused regression, independent implementation review and all 46 full-scene geometry/PNG verdicts before acceptance. Preserve production UI, feature requirements, history, coverage baselines and protected approval gates.\ntype_menu_fixture_correction: Establish viewport (Recommended)\nReason: Exact-head Python 3.13/3.14 snapshots show the focused field at y=-8 above the viewport starting at y=4, with matching type input and populated matches; production positioning explicitly hides such menus. Establishing a settled visible starting viewport corrects this regression's precondition while retaining menu-visible, placement, scroll-out, focus, unchanged-value and no-query assertions. Preserve production positioning and require GitHub validation across supported environments. Both choices retain the complete multicursor/clipboard/caret scope, RPi policy/restart work and root monitoring objective until every task-related PR merges successfully into dev with required validation.","questions":["1. Which correction should the plan specify for the demonstrated target-size picker rendering defect?\nSupersampled export (Recommended): Render the unchanged framed SVG at 2560×1600, then reduce once to 1280×800 with existing Pillow/Lanczos; require GitHub reproduction and full visual review before accepting the repair.\nFurther diagnostic comparison: Keep ordinary capture unchanged and first collect a GitHub comparison of supersampled reduction against current target-size rendering, then independently plan the demonstrated repair.","2. The failing snapshot shows correct menu hiding for an already offscreen field. Should the regression explicitly establish a settled, visible starting viewport before testing scroll-out behavior?\nEstablish viewport (Recommended): Settle expanded layout, focus the field, scroll it into view without animation, and assert its starting geometry before retaining all menu-visible and scroll-out assertions; preserve production positioning.\nTrace scroll origin first: Add bounded GitHub observations around expansion and focus to identify who scrolls the field offscreen before choosing a fixture or production change."]},{"choice":"pillow_test_dependency: Test dependencies (Recommended)\nReason: The supersampling regression imports PIL directly, while both GitHub matrix install commands and tox latest/min and coverage dependencies omit Pillow. Adding the existing agent-tool range Pillow>=10,<13 to those test environments and applying assertion-preserving formatting is a bounded correction supported by the owner's recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues. Preserve public dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 compatibility, the complete multicursor/clipboard/caret checkpoint, coverage/debt baselines, authenticated history, independent reviews, full-scene visual review and required exact-head GitHub checks. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This selection supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which bounded correction should the plan specify for the current-head Pillow collection failure and Ruff formatting finding?\nTest dependencies (Recommended): Add Pillow>=10,<13 to both GitHub matrix install commands, tox latest/min test dependencies and tox coverage dependencies; format supersampled_capture.py while preserving all assertions, public dependencies, feature changes and review gates.\nShared test requirements: Introduce a shared test-only Pillow requirements file consumed by those GitHub and tox environments, with the same compatibility range, formatting correction and preserved assertions; this adds a new dependency-management file."]},{"choice":"history_retention_strategy: Shared lifecycle (Recommended)\nReason: The request requires complete multicursor editing and undo/redo semantics and fixing issues encountered. Source confirms cursor edits prune metadata against live undo/redo edits, while indentation appends records without that pruning. Shared recording/pruning, reset cleanup, and regressions for repeated indentation/undo, discarded redo branches, eviction and reset address this defect without reducing feature scope. Preserve cursor selections and preferred columns for live history, the complete checkpoint and authenticated history, GitHub-only validation, independent implementation review, full-scene visual review, coverage/debt baselines and applicable real-owner protected approvals. Retain the RPi recommendation-policy/restart work and root monitoring objective until every task-related PR merges successfully into dev with required validation. This selects an implementation approach only; it grants no plan, code, visual, protected-policy or merge approval.","questions":["1. Which correction should the renewed plan specify for the verified cursor-history retention defect, while preserving the complete feature checkpoint and all review gates?\nShared lifecycle (Recommended): Share recording/pruning across cursor edits and indentation, retain metadata only for live undo/redo edits, clear obsolete records on document resets, and add fast regressions for repeated indent/undo, discarded redo branches, history eviction and reset."]},{"choice":"reset_and_fixture_correction: Reset state (Recommended)\nReason: The request requires complete multicursor editing semantics and fixing encountered issues; the standing policy supports this routine recommended correction. Current load_text clears history snapshots but retains secondary selections and preferred columns. Clearing obsolete cursor state before replacement while preserving Textual’s primary reset behavior addresses that defect. Mounted reset/render/type regressions and complete idle/EditHistory fixtures support validation without weakening assertions. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, clipboard/caret requirements, history lifecycle, compatibility and coverage baselines. Require GitHub-only validation, fresh independent plan and implementation review, and full-scene visual review bound to the corrected candidate; published-head evidence cannot validate unpublished edits. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This resolves the choice only and grants no plan, source, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which bounded correction should the renewed plan specify for the verified stale-cursor reset defect and the two CI fixture failures?\nReset state (Recommended): Clear secondary selections and old preferred columns before document replacement, preserve Textual’s primary reset behavior, add mounted reset/render/type regressions, complete the idle test double, and supply all required EditHistory constructor arguments.\nReconcile cursors: Clamp and merge existing cursors into the replacement document instead of clearing them, with explicit retained-cursor tests and the same two CI fixture corrections."]},{"choice":"unmounted_reset_context: Active app context (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix encountered issues support this bounded test-context correction. The existing unmounted reset test constructs two detached editors outside an app context, while neighboring history regressions use asyncio.run and SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession()).run_test(). Providing that context while explicitly preserving both editors' unmounted state and every construction/reset/history assertion retains the required regression coverage without changing production behavior. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, multicursor/clipboard/caret requirements, coverage baselines, GitHub-only validation, independent reviews and full visual gate. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This choice supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which correction should the renewed plan specify for the four unmounted-reset failures at head a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1?\nActive app context (Recommended): Run the existing parameterized test through asyncio.run and SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession()).run_test(); keep both new editors detached, explicitly assert they remain unmounted, preserve every construction/reset/history assertion, and leave production behavior unchanged."]},{"choice":"native_caret_correction: Native styling (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated whitespace correction requires preserving every in-document character, expanded-tab cell, color and width while using thin underlines, with bars reserved for padding. Neutralizing native cursor styling after CSS resolution, preserving original theme state and retaining strict real-renderer assertions directly supports that requirement; inspected published-head PNGs still show block styling. Behavior-preserving formatting and reconciliation with pinned dev also support fixing encountered issues: current controller/documentation diffs remove newer provenance and notification safeguards, which must be preserved. Retain the complete multicursor, clipboard, history and narrow UI checkpoint, coverage/debt baselines, GitHub-only execution, fresh independent plan and implementation reviews, exact-head CI and all 46 geometry/full-PNG verdicts. Historical captures do not validate saved edits. Preserve companion policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. Any remaining protected-path change requires the real owner's applicable exact-head approval; this choice supplies none.","questions":["1. Should the renewed plan correct native primary-caret styling before the existing underline overlay, retain strict real-renderer color assertions, fix the reported formatting, and reconcile stale controller/test/documentation changes with pinned dev while preserving the complete feature?\nNative styling (Recommended): Neutralize native cursor colors through a render-only theme after CSS resolution, preserve original theme state and cell colors, strengthen mounted regressions, and require fresh independent review plus GitHub CI and all 46 visual scenes."]},{"choice":"connections_border_scope: Diagnose border gaps (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommended-options policy and instruction to fix encountered issues support bounded evidence-led investigation of this reported visual blocker. The choice establishes neither a border defect nor its cause: obtain actual candidate-bound widget/compositor/SVG/full-PNG evidence through an authorized GitHub route, then independently plan only a demonstrated narrow repair with meaningful regressions. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, selected mount-ordering and six paired caret comparisons, ruler reassessment, all assertions, coverage/debt floors, independent reviews and all 46 geometry/full-PNG gates. Missing generated diagnostics remain coordinator acquisition prerequisites, not owner questions. Retain companion obligations and monitoring of every qualifying PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This selection grants no whole-plan, source, visual, protected exact-head, deployment or merge approval and releases no operational hold.","questions":["1. Should the renewed plan include evidence-led diagnosis and a narrow repair of the reported connections-searching dialog/results border gaps, preserving the complete feature, selected mount/caret work and ruler reassessment? The report does not yet establish the failing layer.\nDiagnose border gaps (Recommended): Obtain candidate-bound widget/compositor/SVG/full-PNG evidence, then independently plan only the demonstrated border repair; retain all assertions and full-scene gates."]},{"choice":"current_head_correction: Scoped alignment (Recommended)\nReason: The retained Narrow gate repairs decision explicitly includes restoring intended new-file centering. The inspected full PNG shows upper-left placement; settled geometry records the dialog at (0,0), resolved screen alignment left/top and no pending layout. Source declares center/middle for NewFileScreen and identifies NewSqlFileScreen as its subclass. Explicitly including that subclass in the existing selector, with mounted centering and resize regressions, is a supported narrow correction. Assigned GitHub logs also substantiate Ruff findings; behavior-preserving fixes must retain diagnostic output, fixture bytes, assertions, negative controls and coverage/debt floors. Preserve the complete selection/multicursor/clipboard/caret/history checkpoint, mount ordering, comparison and border diagnostics, ruler reassessment, selected repairs and current-dev safeguards. Historical evidence cannot validate edits against dev b82ddee4248051c562f3f655e93425aeb32e1885: require fresh complete-plan and implementation review, exact-head GitHub validation and all 46 candidate-bound geometry/full-PNG verdicts. Continue companion obligations and monitoring every qualifying PR through successful dev merge and required validation. No owner fact, whole-plan/source/visual approval, protected exact-head approval, hold release or merge clearance is supplied.","questions":["1. Should the correction explicitly apply NewFileScreen’s existing center/middle alignment to its NewSqlFileScreen subclass, and make only behavior-preserving fixes for the reported Ruff findings? The current PNG and settled geometry show the subclass at (0,0) with resolved left/top alignment, while the base source declares center/middle.\nScoped alignment (Recommended): Add the subclass to the existing alignment selector, cover actual mounted centering and resize behavior, preserve all feature/diagnostic work and assertions, and require fresh independent review plus GitHub validation."]},{"choice":"renderer_ci_provisioning: Provision existing gates (Recommended)\nReason: The recorded Faithful export underlines strategy requires a real raster regression without skips, including canonical coverage and the required runtime matrix. Test-only resvg-py>=0.5,<0.6 matches the existing renderer requirement; provisioning fontconfig/DejaVu on GitHub supports that validation without selecting a production font. Preserve current-dev safeguards, Python 3.9–3.14/minimum profiles, public Python 3.8 static compatibility, all assertions and coverage/debt floors. Installation compatibility, font observations and causal raster results must be established by fresh GitHub execution, never assumed. Retain the complete feature checkpoint, twelve stage comparisons, independent complete-plan/source review, all 46 visual verdicts, genuine authority gates and monitoring of every qualifying PR through successful dev merge and required validation. No local execution, native deployment, protected approval or whole-plan approval is granted.","questions":["1. Should the plan provision the real raster regression in every ordinary test environment, so it runs without skips under the existing required matrix and coverage gates?\nProvision existing gates (Recommended): Add test-only resvg-py>=0.5,<0.6 beside Pillow in tox latest/minimum/coverage and both GitHub installs; provision fontconfig/DejaVu on GitHub and run the real regression explicitly before the full suite."]},{"choice":"lossless_svg_fixture_storage: Preserve captured bytes (Recommended)\nReason: Lossless base64 fixture storage addresses whitespace findings while preserving the required unmodified captured SVG inputs. Validate decoding against the existing original SHA256 hashes before raster replay; preserve provenance, every causal assertion and negative control, and distinguish envelope hashes from decoded-source hashes. Update only storage paths/loaders and the extra EOF blank line. Retain the complete feature checkpoint, GitHub-only validation, independent plan/source/visual reviews, all twelve stage comparisons, all 46 scene verdicts, current-dev safeguards and qualifying-PR monitoring through successful dev merges and required validation. This choice supplies no raster result, protected approval or whole-plan approval.","questions":["1. Should the plan replace the two tracked SVG fixtures with lossless base64 JSON envelopes to resolve the whitespace findings while preserving the exact captured SVG bytes used by the real raster regression?\nPreserve captured bytes (Recommended): Store exact SVG bytes in whitespace-clean JSON, decode with validation before replay, preserve original decoded hashes/provenance, update fixture paths/loaders, and remove only the extra EOF blank line in underline_geometry.py."]}],"images":[],"plans":[{"approval_index":0,"id":"cf25c1a4d6a8bb36186ff70e6f5ad9dd930414b0e4e2a7426f5a5236986ba29a","text":"# SQL Explorer selection, multicursor clipboard, and thin carets\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd continuous selection with Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down, reproduce VS Code’s multicursor paste distribution, and render every editor caret as a thin vertical bar. Keep your explicit override: empty selections copy empty fragments.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Bind Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down to extend each existing selection by one logical line without adding cursors. Preserve its anchor and preferred column, clamp on short lines, and restore that column on longer lines. Reversing direction shrinks the selection and can cross its anchor. Keep Shift+Up/Down as the existing add-cursor shortcuts.\n- Store multicursor clipboard metadata alongside the plain clipboard text: one fragment per selection in document order, including empty fragments and embedded newlines. Export joined plain text through the existing system clipboard and OSC 52 transports.\n- Follow [VS Code’s paste distribution](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/main/src/vs/editor/common/cursor/cursorTypeEditOperations.ts): distribute stored fragments when their count matches the destination cursor count; otherwise distribute clipboard lines when their count matches, ignoring one trailing line ending. If neither matches, insert the whole clipboard at every cursor. A single destination receives the joined text.\n- Apply fragments by destination document order, rather than attaching them permanently to cursor identities. Invalidate stored metadata on another Explorer copy or when received clipboard text differs.\n- Route Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V, `cp`/`pst`, cut, and terminal paste through shared clipboard handling. Leave query execution’s selected-text collection separate. Copying with all selections empty clears the clipboard; pasting an empty clipboard does nothing.\n- Extend the existing batch-edit mechanism to accept distinct insertions while preserving cursor positions and one-step undo/redo.\n- Replace block caret rendering with a non-bold vertical bar for active and secondary cursors, including unfocused, empty-line, and end-of-line carets. The bar temporarily covers its terminal cell without changing document text.\n- Update Explorer’s editing documentation and add the required changelog fragment. No public package API changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Test repeated vertical selection, direction reversal, short/empty lines, document boundaries, existing multicursors, and unchanged add-cursor shortcuts.\n- Test distinct and multiline fragments, mixed/all-empty selections, changed cursor counts, recreated cursors, external line spreading, full-text fallback, clipboard replacement, and single-cursor paste.\n- Verify keyboard, command, cut, terminal-paste, clipboard-fallback, and undo/redo paths.\n- Verify bar carets with syntax highlighting, selections, scrolling, and focus changes.\n- Run focused and mandatory precommit checks. Complete the full SQL Explorer headless visual review, inspecting every scene before commit.\n\n## Delivery and defaults\n\nAfter leaving Plan mode, create the session-owned feature branch through the managed workflow and revalidate against incoming changes. Implement, validate, and publish a PR to `dev`.\n\nVS Code parity applies to the requested selection and clipboard behavior; retain existing Explorer shortcuts. Your empty-selection rule takes precedence over VS Code’s default line-copy behavior.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"48a661e2fd3a2309b243f9ec0fb10cf92f3d305e7ad8d345b1de83600ff2c620","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and complete picker diagnosis on current dev\n\n## Summary\n\nRevalidate the complete saved correction against pinned dev `0b26a608bba00ff1bf29bde578b436aa817eab14`. Preserve the multicursor feature and useful checkpoint changes, resolve both merge conflicts through the approved coder, and validate the already-selected four-way picker comparison.\n\nNo additional owner choices are needed for this step. The verified PNG shows an obscured `c`; the supplied SVGs retain the complete heading. The rendering cause remains unproven, so this plan authorizes diagnosis, not a speculative presentation repair.\n\n## Merge recovery and compatibility\n\n- In `.github/agent/task_context.py`, resolve both conflicts to the pinned base’s behavior: retain `Path`, `ARCHIVE_MARKER`, and oversized inline evidence returning `None` so publication can use the archive transport. The resolved file should match pinned dev exactly; preserve complete history and existing provenance checks.\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, combine both sides of both conflicts, retaining distinct feature and current-dev entries and all historical release sections. Remove only conflict markers and exact duplicate entries.\n- Retain the existing task fragment as one concise `- ` bullet; it already satisfies the reported format requirement. Do not change package or README versions.\n- Preserve recovered diagnostic tests and README content. Fully read files before editing; compare against the immutable pre24 originals and retain every original test method, the recovered suffix, and useful diagnostic additions.\n- Preserve public package APIs, existing creation shortcuts, clipboard transports, and supported Python/Textual compatibility. The picker comparison is an additive diagnostic JSON interface.\n\n## Feature requirements to retain\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Support independent cursor positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, editing, and one-step undo/redo. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard; cut deletes nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste uses matching recorded fragments first, matching clipboard lines second, and whole-text repetition otherwise. Ignore one trailing line ending for line spreading. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share these rules; changed clipboard text invalidates fragment metadata.\n- Keep SQL readable: supported vertical bars where possible, thin underlines in occupied cells, and visible primary and secondary carets.\n- Retain only the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs: scene consistency and Cancel focus, create-table controls and menu placement, help wrapping, find-highlight visibility, and evidence-led picker diagnosis.\n\n## Diagnostic implementation and focused coverage\n\nPreserve and finish the existing integration between `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py` and `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`, with regressions in `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`.\n\n- For database-picker only, retain `raw_original`, `framed_original`, `raw_dejavu`, and `framed_dejavu` in geometry JSON from one final export. Reuse the ordinary PNG for `framed_original`.\n- Change only the terminal matrix font-family declaration in diagnostic font variants to verified-available DejaVu Sans Mono. Preserve production rendering, text, positions, clips, title fonts, and framing.\n- Retain exact UTF-8 SVG strings, lossless base64 PNGs, lengths, SHA256 hashes, observed dimensions, renderer arguments, versions, and font observations.\n- Keep separate 4 MiB combined comparison SVG and decoded PNG limits. Missing fonts, ambiguous declarations, renderer failures, or omitted content must mark comparisons incomplete. System font matches must never be described as renderer-selected fonts.\n- Keep atomic geometry publication and the existing artifact route; do not modify the protected capture workflow.\n- Run fast, service-free regressions covering lossless encoding, exact boundaries, unavailable/fallback fonts, declaration-only changes, partial failures, ordinary-PNG reuse, picker-only integration, and preserved geometry/readiness gates.\n- Recheck multicursor, selection/clipboard, caret, button-style, selector, completion, and capture-lifecycle suites. Historical CI identified disabled-button color failures and lint findings; verify their current corrections on the new candidate without weakening assertions or debt baselines.\n\n## GitHub validation and completion\n\n- Private planning/coding workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. GitHub performs focused checks, mandatory static/coverage/artifact/matrix validation, and captures.\n- Obtain independent plan review covering the new base, both conflict resolutions, and the complete preserved task before coding.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route to capture all 46 scenes and the four picker comparisons. Bind artifacts to the exact candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan; coordinator extraction must verify decoded bytes and hashes.\n- Independently inspect all four comparison images before selecting a repair. Incomplete or inconclusive comparisons require further diagnosis and renewed planning. A successful capture is not visual approval.\n- Once evidence establishes the cause, obtain a concrete reviewed repair plan, add a focused regression, and repeat full-scene capture. Every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict must pass before correction publication.\n- Require fresh implementation review and required checks for the final published head and current dev base. Preserve credentials, owner vetoes, provenance, and any applicable exact-head protected approval.\n- The coordinator retains responsibility for recommendation-policy companion review, safe activation, and recovery of waiting agents while preserving genuine-input/security holds.\n- Monitor SQL Explorer PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and all task-related repair PRs through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that root objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"7ff002c5964b2e8a254e39d777cc20399ff3b70586fc5e3cc917aedf80f0f827","text":"# Correct PR #9 CI while preserving SQL Explorer requirements\n\n## Summary\n\nCorrect the failures bound to head `0a943f8c16643228436a2bcbc23b02fbe2f28cff` in GitHub run `38889674199`, against pinned dev `0b26a608bba00ff1bf29bde578b436aa817eab14`.\n\nThe immutable logs establish two causes: invalid plain-color parsing in the disabled-button regression and new Ruff findings in the SVG diagnostic helper/tests. The resolver selected the CSS-reference approach; that selection supplies no implementation, visual, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/button_styles.py`, remove the `Color.parse(palette[\"text-disabled\"])` override from `DisabledColorReference`. Let its existing `color: $text-disabled` CSS resolve through Textual after mounting beside the tested button.\n- Retain strict comparisons of resolved foreground/background, automatic-color state, and rendered Rich foreground/background. Preserve the deliberate incorrect-color negative control, cleanup, hover/focus checks, removal-control legibility, and both advanced-panel states.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py`, correct the reported FURB167, PERF401, two PLR2004 findings, and unused RUF100 suppression using equivalent expressions, named limits, and removal of only the unused suppression. Preserve iteration order and exact diagnostic contents.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`, fix all four E501 findings and Ruff formatting through layout changes and adjacent string literals that preserve fixture bytes. Retain every test and assertion.\n- Keep public APIs, dependency declarations, Python 3.8–3.14 support, supported Textual versions, diagnostic schema/version, hashes, encodings, and separate 4 MiB SVG/decoded-PNG limits unchanged. Preserve the existing changelog history and record the correction through the managed fragment mechanism without a package-version bump.\n- Fully read each edited file through `has_more=false`; preserve recovered diagnostic tests, documentation, and the complete checkpoint. Do not reset the feature or modify lint/type debt baselines.\n\n## Requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Retain independent cursor positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, and one-step undo/redo. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard; cut deletes nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second—ignoring one trailing line ending—and otherwise repeat the whole text. Changed clipboard text invalidates metadata; empty paste does nothing.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible primary/secondary thin carets: supported vertical bars where possible, thin underlines in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow fixture/UI repairs and evidence-led picker diagnosis. Preserve four-way raw/framed, original/DejaVu comparison evidence, ordinary-PNG reuse, atomic geometry publication, and explicit incomplete results. This CI correction does not select a picker presentation or rasterization repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers only inspect or edit source.\n\n- First run the button-style module on minimum and current Textual environments. Require both advanced-panel states to pass for every button, with strict rendered-color comparisons and negative controls still detecting incorrect colors.\n- Run SVG-evidence tests with fake font probes/renderers: verify exact bytes/hashes, font-declaration-only changes, exact limit boundaries, unavailable/fallback fonts, partial failures, PNG dimensions, ordinary-PNG reuse, picker-only integration, and readiness/geometry rejection.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, movement, caret, selector/completion, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type checks, coverage ratchets, artifact smoke tests, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and the aggregate fast-check gate. Preserve all assertions and baselines.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for full-scene capture. Bind artifacts to candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, and reviewed content; independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass before correction publication.\n- Preserve the picker comparison review prerequisite wherever unresolved. Successful capture or green CI alone does not establish its cause or visual approval; a demonstrated repair requires a concrete renewed plan, focused regression, and full visual review.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding, then independent implementation review for the resulting head and current dev base. Revalidate if dev changes.\n- Preserve complete authenticated task history and provenance through trusted publication transport. Coordinator tooling gaps remain coordinator-owned; do not truncate history.\n- Keep protected workflows unchanged for this correction. Any later protected-path change requires the real owner’s applicable exact-head approval; recommendation selection cannot substitute.\n- The coordinator must complete the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and safely restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving genuine-input, credential, provenance, and owner-veto holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related correction/repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This bounded CI correction does not complete that root objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"b3631dec6cfa7592c57086a4b15a7092ff53c6453c44ec3db30371479476aa73","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and complete the evidence-first correction\n\n## Summary\n\nRevalidate the complete saved patch against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`. Only the approved coder may resolve conflicts or edit source.\n\nPreserve the selected evidence-first sequence: reconcile the changelog, finish behavior-preserving lint corrections and bounded diagnostics, then obtain exact-candidate GitHub evidence before specifying a production checkbox or picker repair. No additional owner decision is needed for this step.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Resolve every conflict in `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, including the new top conflict and nested older markers. Use pinned dev’s release history as the skeleton; retain all distinct feature and dev entries, removing conflict markers and exact duplicate entries only. Preserve historical release sections and package/README versions.\n- Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, recovered test/documentation content, authenticated chronological history, and existing task fragment. Fully read each file through its final page before editing.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py`, verify the saved correction addresses the reported BLE001/RUF100 findings while retaining renderer-failure containment and explicit incomplete evidence. Apply canonical formatting to its tests without changing fixture bytes, diagnostic contents, limits, hashes, or assertions.\n- Retain the existing checkbox diagnostics and regressions, particularly `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py`. On strict form assertion failure, report the original snapshot without recollecting: checkbox value/label, direct render, widget/compositor rows, styles, ancestor geometry/clips, advanced-panel state, and runtime versions. Keep output bounded and explicitly identify missing or truncated observations.\n- Preserve public package interfaces, Python 3.8–3.14 and supported Textual compatibility. Diagnostic JSON remains additive. Do not change dependencies, protected workflows, coverage targets, debt baselines, production checkbox presentation, or picker rendering in this diagnostic step.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors; preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, short lines, and boundaries.\n- Retain multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, atomic undo/redo, and Shift+Up/Down toggling at the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share the rules; changed clipboard text invalidates metadata.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported, underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs and unresolved picker comparison prerequisite. Partial code supplies no additional scope authorization.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nAll programs, tests, font probes, and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- Exercise checkbox diagnostics across checked/unchecked, enabled/disabled, focused/unfocused, and collapsed/expanded states. Preserve strict full-label assertions and negative controls detecting widget or compositor text loss; verify bounded failures do not mutate or recollect evidence.\n- Run the failing advanced create-table scene first on Python 3.14/latest dependencies and the canonical coverage environment. Preserve diagnostics from the actual failing state, with exact source and dependency bindings.\n- Run SVG comparison tests covering lossless bytes/hashes, declaration-only font changes, limits, unavailable fonts, renderer failures, ordinary-PNG reuse, and explicit incomplete results.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, movement/history, caret, button-color, selector/completion, type-menu containment, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Obtain exact-candidate coverage JSON through the coordinator. Historical run `38897073714` missed branch and combined ratchets; use current missing lines/arcs to target meaningful task-related regressions. Do not weaken assertions or lower targets.\n- Preserve four picker comparisons—raw/framed with original/DejaVu declarations—through bounded geometry JSON. Verify decoded hashes and independently inspect all four images. System font matching does not establish the renderer-selected font.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review covering pinned dev, all changelog conflict resolutions, and the complete preserved task before coding.\n- Require exact-candidate static/lint/format/type checks, coverage ratchets, artifact checks, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate route for diagnosis and all 46 full-scene captures. Bind artifacts to candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan.\n- After checkbox and picker evidence identifies the first failing layer, produce concrete repair plans for independent review before production changes. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved.\n- Require independent implementation review and passing geometry checks plus individual full-PNG verdicts before publishing a correction. Revalidate against subsequent dev changes.\n- Preserve credentials, owner vetoes, provenance, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Recommendation resolution does not replace those approvals.\n- The coordinator retains the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, preserving genuine-input and security holds, and monitors PR #9 plus every task-related companion/repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a7fdaee407cb54717777ca2d6fc954e553bb44ab2e0ca1979ff9dc8db8d501d6","text":"# Correct PR #9 CI and preserve the complete SQL Explorer task\n\n## Summary\n\nCorrect the verified failures for head `49a16ba6f44cfa30e986aa62cec96ad0de9f47e0` in GitHub run `38915766002`, against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe resolver selected the complete-fixture approach. No further implementation choice is outstanding for this bounded correction. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint and evidence-first sequence; picker repair remains dependent on comparison evidence.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/selector_diagnostics.py`, mount a real `Collapsible` with ID `create-table-advanced` after the existing Select. Keep the selector’s default geometry and all completeness, full-row, label, arrow, and visibility assertions. Assert that the collected collapsed state matches the mounted panel. Retain the separate missing-panel negative control.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`, extract the per-region loop body into a private helper accepting the target, composed strips, result, and remaining row budget, and returning the updated budget. Preserve target order, entry insertion order, checkbox observations, invisible-region handling, row consumption, exception containment, limits, and missing/omission messages. Keep scene setup and final visibility checks in `terminal_diagnostics`; resolve PLR0912 without adding a suppression.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py` and `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`. Preserve every test, assertion, fixture byte, hash expectation, and diagnostic limit.\n- Fully read each edited file through its final page before writing. Preserve recovered source/documentation and existing changelog history; record the correction through the managed fragment mechanism.\n- Keep public APIs, diagnostic JSON shape, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 support, supported Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n\n## Feature and diagnostic requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down cursor toggling.\n- Preserve document-order clipboard fragments for Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve paste precedence: matching fragments, then matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share the rules; changed clipboard text invalidates metadata and empty paste does nothing.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible thin primary/secondary carets, using vertical bars where supported and underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs. Preserve checkbox failing-state diagnostics without recollection and the unresolved four-way picker comparisons: raw/framed SVG with original/DejaVu terminal-font declarations, exact hashes, lossless bounded geometry-JSON transport, and explicit incomplete results.\n- This correction changes no production checkbox or picker presentation. Select any further repair only after evidence establishes its cause and a concrete repair plan receives independent review.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- First run selector diagnostics in minimum and current Textual environments. Require the repaired fixture’s complete child rows and advanced context to pass, while missing, hidden, clipped, zero-height, and concealed-child controls still detect failures.\n- Run checkbox and render-diagnostic regressions covering checked/disabled/focused/advanced states, original-snapshot preservation, missing context, invisible regions, row/region/cell limits, and collection failures. Preserve exact diagnostic behavior through the helper extraction.\n- Run SVG-evidence and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, button-color, selector/completion, and type-menu checks.\n- Require fresh exact-candidate lint/format/type checks, canonical coverage and ratchets, artifact smoke tests, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks. The current coverage job stopped at the fixture failure; it does not establish a new coverage shortfall. Obtain coverage JSON through the coordinator before selecting any additional coverage correction.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate route for all 46 scenes and four picker comparisons. Bind artifacts to the candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan; verify extracted hashes and independently inspect comparison images. Successful capture alone establishes neither a repair cause nor visual approval.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and independent implementation review for the resulting head and dev base. Revalidate if dev changes.\n- Require every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict to pass before correction publication. Unresolved picker evidence remains a blocker requiring further diagnosis.\n- Preserve complete authenticated task history, provenance, credentials, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Resolver selection supplies no such approval.\n- The coordinator completes the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and safely restarts agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving genuine-input and security holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This CI correction is an intermediate step toward that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"358507414a8d1e59404d2fdc5ecbc61d9c704ed103e2afa7cb3d520108a62050","text":"# Preserve PR #9 and collect decisive correction evidence\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2` against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe four inspected picker images locate heading degradation at the framing boundary: raw images retain the `c`; framed images obscure it with either font. Framing changes serialization and scale together, so neither is yet established as the cause. The original coverage JSON and pre-assert menu trace were not retained.\n\nImplement a bounded diagnostic checkpoint, then independently plan the demonstrated repairs. No additional owner preference is needed for this sequence.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Preserve the complete feature patch, recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, original approvals, and chronological questions and answers. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py`, preserving every assertion, fixture value, and negative control.\n- Instrument `tests/sql/explorer/type_menu_viewport.py` with a test-support snapshot collected immediately before its existing initial visibility assertion and after scrolling. Capture focused-widget identity, field focus/mount state, `type_input` identity, matches/index/accepted type, menu visibility, scroll offsets, field/menu/viewport geometry, advanced-panel state, and dependency versions.\n- Read queued-message counts and pending layout/refresh flags only where observable; mark unavailable probes explicitly. Bound each snapshot to 8 KiB, reporting omissions. Attach the original snapshot to assertion failures without recollection, event draining, retries, refocusing, or changing assertion order.\n- Extend the SVG evidence helper and database-picker capture integration with three diagnostic controls: XML-reserialized raw SVG at native size; a target-size frame preserving the original SVG interior bytes; and the existing XML frame at native viewBox dimensions. Preserve the original four comparisons and ordinary production PNG.\n- Retain exact SVG inputs, lossless PNGs, dimensions, renderer settings, versions, hashes, and explicit failures through additive geometry JSON. Count all comparisons toward the existing separate 4 MiB SVG and decoded-PNG budgets. Do not change production framing, picker presentation, font selection, or dependencies.\n- In `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, add an `always()` artifact upload after the quality job’s existing command for generated `coverage.json`, using a unique run/head-bound artifact name. Preserve command exit status and existing check requirements; explicitly report when no JSON was generated. Keep protected capture/controller workflows unchanged.\n- Document the diagnostic route briefly and record the correction through the managed changelog fragment mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Compatibility and retained behavior\n\nPublic package APIs and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support remain unchanged. Diagnostic interfaces are additive.\n\nRetain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n\nRetain document-order copy/cut fragments, empty multicursor clipboard clearing, whole-buffer single-cursor copy, and paste precedence of matching fragments, matching lines, then whole-text repetition. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling and clipboard invalidation.\n\nKeep readable SQL with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback. Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs and RPi recommendation-policy/restart objective.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Test snapshot completeness, unavailable probes, truncation, serialization, and preservation of focus, queues, scroll, and menu state. Preserve the visible-menu, offscreen-menu, unchanged-value, and no-query assertions.\n- Run the instrumented menu regression first on Python 3.13/3.14 and canonical Python 3.11, retaining actual failures and dependency bindings.\n- Test diagnostic SVG controls for preserved text, styles, clips, coordinates, fonts, exact bytes/hashes, dimensions, limits, and partial failures using fake renderers. Verify ordinary capture output remains unchanged.\n- Obtain fresh canonical coverage JSON through the artifact route. Keep the **98.03% branch floor** and all debt/coverage baselines. Select additional task-related regression cases only from the actual new missing arcs.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, checkbox, selector/completion, and capture-lifecycle suites, followed by required lint, format, type, coverage, artifact, compatibility, SDK, and aggregate fast checks.\n\n## Review and completion\n\nObtain fresh independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward. Bind new diagnostics and captures to their actual candidate, source, dependencies, task, plan, and GitHub run.\n\nIndependently inspect the new picker controls and menu observations before specifying production repairs. Inconclusive results require renewed diagnosis; successful capture supplies no visual approval. After a concrete repair plan and implementation, recapture all 46 scenes and require every geometry check and individual full-PNG verdict before correction publication.\n\nPreserve credentials, provenance, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. Revalidate against subsequent dev changes.\n\nThe coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, preserving genuine-input and security holds, and monitor PR #9 plus all task-related companion/repair PRs through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a294f7d30580917dcca0900f202cc27955c1445ac0c53df2dd3f1c5acb11fa10","text":"# Correct PR #9 rendering and CI while preserving the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `7756937e843fe7ffcc30ab0c0ba2a58bf7d7cee2`, against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nThe complete current-head check records and failed-job logs identify lint, menu-fixture, coverage, and picker-rendering blockers. Seven inspected picker controls isolate heading degradation to target-size rendering; serialization-only and native-size framing preserve it.\n\nThe independent resolver selected supersampled export and an explicitly visible starting viewport. These choices require fresh plan review and validation; they establish no implementation or visual approval.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, original approvals, and chronological questions and answers. Fully read every edited file through its final continuation before writing. Revalidate against incoming dev changes.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`, render every ordinary capture at **2560×1600**, then reduce once to **1280×800** using existing Pillow’s `Image.Resampling.LANCZOS`. Preserve the 208×47 terminal grid, framing, aspect ratio, fonts, SVG contents, and production UI.\n- Put the shared rasterization helper in the SVG-evidence module. Scale the unchanged framed SVG using an outer SVG viewport with `viewBox=\"0 0 1280 800\"` and dimensions 2560×1600. Validate intermediate and final dimensions; propagate rendering failures instead of silently reverting to the rejected path.\n- Preserve all seven existing diagnostic controls as direct-render comparisons. Render `framed_original` independently rather than reusing the newly processed ordinary PNG. Add a separately identified supersampled comparison that reuses the ordinary final PNG.\n- Extend additive geometry evidence to retain the exact supersampling SVG, renderer settings, intermediate dimensions/hash, final dimensions/hash, Pillow version, and reduction filter. Preserve raw/framed inputs and distinguish direct rendering from the processed output. Keep the existing separate 4 MiB SVG and decoded-PNG budgets, explicit incomplete results, hash verification, and atomic geometry publication.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/type_menu_viewport.py`, settle the expanded layout, focus the type field, scroll it into view without animation, and settle before entering the existing assertion sequence. Assert that the field is inside the viewport with room below it. Preserve menu visibility/placement, subsequent scroll-out hiding, retained focus, unchanged values, and no-query assertions. Keep production positioning unchanged.\n- Resolve PERF203 in the menu-diagnostics support module by extracting package-version lookup and exception handling into a helper. Preserve observation order, missing-version reporting, snapshot contents, and non-mutating behavior.\n- Correct the five E501 findings and formatting in checkbox diagnostics, and formatting in the SVG-evidence helper. Preserve fixture bytes, assertions, negative controls, diagnostic limits, and exception containment.\n- Document the capture pipeline briefly and record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Feature and compatibility requirements\n\n- Retain anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without creating cursors, independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and document boundaries.\n- Retain independent positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, atomic editing/history, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste retain matching-fragment precedence, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: supported vertical bars with occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs. Existing partial code grants no additional scope.\n- Keep public package APIs, dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged. Renderer evidence changes remain additive.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Add fast rasterization tests using a fake SVG renderer and small in-memory images: exact input preservation, doubled dimensions, one Lanczos reduction, final dimensions, failure propagation, accurate hashes/settings, and correct ordinary-PNG reuse. Retain comparison limits, omission/failure controls, and capture-readiness rejection tests.\n- Run the repaired menu regression first on Python 3.13/3.14 and canonical Python 3.11, plus minimum/current Textual environments. Preserve bounded failure snapshots without recollection or assertion retries.\n- Use the retained coverage report from run `38943147406` to add meaningful editor regressions for its actual missing branches: unmounted idle handling, rendering without a theme, and a search highlight wholly clipped horizontally. Assert safe lifecycle handling, restored theme state, unchanged text/cell widths, and correct visible highlighting.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement/history, caret, checkbox, selector/completion, menu-observation, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type checks, canonical coverage JSON and ratchets, artifact smoke tests, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and aggregate fast checks. Preserve the **98.03% branch floor** and existing combined floor.\n- Obtain an isolated GitHub candidate capture bound to source, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and run. Inspect the repaired picker and all comparison PNGs, then every one of the 46 full scenes. Require all geometry assertions and individual visual verdicts to pass before correction publication. Supersampling is accepted only if the actual heading is readable; otherwise retain the rejection and renew diagnosis.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain independent plan review before coding and implementation review afterward. Revalidate changed heads and dev bases; preserve complete provenance and authenticated history.\n- Preserve credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator completes and safely activates the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restarts agents waiting solely on routine choices, preserving security and genuine-input holds.\n- Monitor SQL Explorer PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related correction/repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. Completing this correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"6b729f400f170ad12628c5a3e1de801ef212a6789ad7f0b6f9f4509a882b0eeb","text":"# Correct PR #9 test dependencies and formatting\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `cfa19a96f14c57203dc328d8fe797018ba53cc0c` against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback and failed-job logs establish two blockers: missing Pillow during test collection and a Ruff formatting finding. The resolver selected the bounded test-dependency correction. No further implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, add quoted `\"Pillow>=10,<13\"` to both latest and minimum matrix installation commands.\n- In `tox.ini`, add the same requirement to latest/minimum test dependencies and explicitly to coverage dependencies, which override the shared list. Preserve SDK-only environments.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/supersampled_capture.py`. Preserve every assertion, fixture, failure case, hash expectation and diagnostic limit.\n- Retain unconditional test collection; do not introduce skips or optional-import fallbacks.\n- Preserve public APIs, runtime dependencies, package extras and Python 3.8–3.14 support. Let pip select a compatible Pillow release within the declared range; verify actual versions on GitHub. Keep runtime-only minimum constraints unchanged.\n- Preserve the complete checkpoint, recovered source/documentation, changelog history and authenticated task history. Record this correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n\n## Requirements retained\n\n- Preserve anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, independent preferred columns, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic editing/history and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Preserve document-order copy/cut fragments, empty multicursor clipboard clearing, whole-buffer single-cursor copy and paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal clipboard handling, metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, supported vertical bars and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled export, comparison evidence and strict diagnostics. This correction selects no additional presentation change and grants no visual approval.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- First run the existing supersampled-capture regressions in clean Python 3.8 minimum/latest and canonical Python 3.11 environments. Verify Pillow imports, exact dimensions/hashes, one Lanczos reduction, failure propagation and comparison-budget boundaries.\n- Require Ruff lint/format checks without baseline changes.\n- Run focused SVG-evidence/capture-lifecycle, multicursor, clipboard, movement/history, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox and selector regressions.\n- Require the complete Python 3.8–3.14 matrix, canonical coverage JSON, existing coverage ratchets—including the 98.03% branch floor—type checks, artifact smoke tests, SDK conformance and aggregate fast checks.\n- Collection failure supplies no new coverage result. Use the new exact-head report before planning any further coverage correction.\n- Obtain the required candidate-bound full visual review: inspect the picker and comparisons, then all 46 full PNGs; require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass. Successful capture alone is insufficient.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding and complete independent implementation review afterward; the current reviewer explicitly left remaining source and companion review unfinished.\n- Revalidate against incoming dev changes. Bind checks, captures and reviews to the actual candidate, base, checkpoint, task and plan.\n- Preserve provenance, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains responsibility for completing and safely activating the RPi recommendation-policy/restart work while preserving genuine-input and security holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9 and every task-related companion or repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This CI correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"5af1df680f9f476de3e392cfa42e3787eb049e270f376b23d4aa337ee5d5e613","text":"# Complete PR #9’s history correction and changelog reconciliation\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete feature checkpoint and reconcile it against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nThe saved source already contains the selected shared history lifecycle and focused regressions. The remaining confirmed source correction is the changelog conflict. Validate the existing lifecycle correction without replacing useful work.\n\nComplete check records show successful CI for published head `806f89ee273a598686fe80d7a26a382acee5a47a`; those results do not validate unpublished checkpoint changes. Independent source, companion, and full-scene review remain required. No material owner question remains.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, remove conflict markers at lines 54, 62, and 64. Retain all seven SQL Explorer entries and dev’s replacement-authority entry under Unreleased. Preserve every historical release section and version marker. Check the complete file for additional conflict markers.\n- Preserve `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`’s shared `_record_cursor_edit` and `_prune_cursor_history` implementation. Both cursor editing and indentation must record snapshots through that lifecycle.\n- Retain snapshots only for exact edit objects present in live undo/redo stacks. Preserve active and secondary selections, selection direction, and independent preferred columns for those edits.\n- Preserve pruning after undo/redo, idle maintenance for inherited edits, and no-op transactions. No-op edits must neither create duplicate snapshots nor destroy live redo metadata. Document resets must immediately release obsolete snapshots, including during widget construction.\n- Preserve `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py` and the existing concise task changelog fragment. Make additional lifecycle changes only if source review or GitHub regression results identify a concrete defect.\n- Keep public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility, protected workflows, coverage targets, and debt baselines unchanged.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors; preserve preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal handling, metadata invalidation, and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve readable SQL and thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported, underline fallback in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampled capture pipeline, recovered source/documentation, diagnostic evidence, and authenticated task history. The inspected picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. All execution occurs on GitHub.\n\n- Run cursor-history regressions first: repeated indent/undo/replacement, abandoned redo branches replaced by indentation, unindentation or editing, checkpoint eviction, document reset, explicit history clearing, inherited edits, and no-op preservation.\n- Assert observable text and cursor restoration alongside bounded metadata retention. Retain reversed selections and independent preferred-column checks.\n- Run focused multicursor, clipboard, selection/movement, caret, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, and capture-lifecycle suites.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK, and aggregate checks. Preserve branch **98.03%**, combined **98.92%**, statement **99.22%**, and all subsystem floors.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for all 46 scenes. Bind capture evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies, and base. Independently inspect every full PNG and geometry result before correction publication; retain comparison evidence and explicit incomplete results.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review, then complete independent implementation review covering every diff continuation, diagnostic helper/test, capture/scene change, and companion implementation. Earlier partial review supplies no approval.\n- Revalidate whenever the head or dev base changes. Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes, and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator must complete and safely activate the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices. Record questions with resolver decisions; recommendations do not substitute for protected approval.\n- Monitor PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion work, and every task-related repair PR through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. Completing this bounded correction does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ee81771267af8eec15d44668ff4aa88017da5dbfadea162fa68e370175ffd805","text":"# Correct PR #9 document resets and CI fixtures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `b346d04a90b5edc073a4c384eae98e3150b883f0`, against pinned dev `8955054742d6df6c4700c6e9db815ff3cb9efc3b`.\n\nComplete current-head feedback identifies stale secondary cursors after document replacement and two test-fixture failures. The independent resolver selected **Reset state**. No material question remains; this selection supplies no implementation, visual, merge, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/editor.py`, extend `load_text()` to clear secondary selections, old preferred-column mappings, and cursor-history snapshots **before** calling Textual’s implementation. Preserve Textual’s primary-cursor reset behavior and the existing method signature. Use only state initialized before `super().__init__()`; avoid mount-dependent selection helpers during construction.\n- Preserve shared history recording/pruning for edits and indentation, exact live-edit identity tracking, undo/redo restoration, inherited-edit maintenance, and no-op redo preservation. Keep idle pruning active.\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/cursor_history.py`, construct the eviction-test history with all required arguments: `max_checkpoints=2`, `checkpoint_timer=60.0`, and `checkpoint_max_characters=1000`. Retain explicit transaction checkpoints and every eviction, metadata-bound, text, selection, and preferred-column assertion.\n- Extend its parameterized reset regression for both `load_text()` and the `text` setter. Create mounted cursors and reversed selections across several rows with distinct preferred columns, populate undo and redo, then replace with shorter single-line text and empty text.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/completion_readiness.py`, complete the idle fixture with empty undo/redo stacks, cursor-history metadata, and a callback invoking the real pruning method. Retain assertions that idle reopens retained suggestions and leaves dismissed suggestions closed.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered tests/documentation, changelog history, and authenticated task history. Record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support, protected workflows, and diagnostic interfaces remain unchanged.\n\n## Required behavior retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection preserves independent preferred columns through reversal, short lines, and boundaries without creating cursors.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing supports multiple cursors per row, selection merging, atomic undo/redo, and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste use matching fragments, then matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Keep SQL readable with thin primary/secondary carets, vertical bars where supported and occupied-cell underline fallback.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling, comparison evidence, and strict diagnostics. The inspected published-head picker PNG supplies no reason for another rendering change.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n- Run the two failing modules first on canonical Python 3.11, Python 3.8 minimum dependencies, and Python 3.13/3.14 latest dependencies.\n- Reset regressions must assert one valid primary cursor, no secondary cursors or obsolete preferences, cleared history/snapshots, safe rendering after layout settles, and typing at only the reset cursor. Undo/redo must not resurrect the old document or cursors. Retain constru